# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Secrets - never commit env files or migration script output
# NOTE: .env itself is intentionally NOT ignored here - the Vercel
# deployment for this project builds directly from the committed .env
# (no separate environment variables are configured in Vercel's own
# dashboard yet), so untracking it breaks every production deploy.
# Only VITE_SUPABASE_URL/VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY live in it, both public,
# embedded-in-client-bundle values by design - not secrets. Re-add .env
# to this list only after Vercel's dashboard env vars are configured
# directly, so the build no longer depends on this file.
.env.*
!.env.example
scripts/output/

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
.vercel
.env.local
